and also on Daily Source Code,

1190
00:56:57,060 --> 00:56:59,300
the music business is going to start figuring out

1191
00:56:59,300 --> 00:57:01,380
how to repackage music and sell music.

1192
00:57:01,380 --> 00:57:05,540
And they're going to treat the iPod platform as radio

1193
00:57:05,540 --> 00:57:07,980
and we're gonna get the same benefits.

1194
00:57:07,980 --> 00:57:10,940
We're gonna be able to use unlimited amounts of music

1195
00:57:10,940 --> 00:57:12,980
on the iPod platform.

1196
00:57:12,980 --> 00:57:15,420
Of course, if we start making money,

1197
00:57:15,420 --> 00:57:19,260
then you're gonna have to pay some of that in royalty fees

1198
00:57:19,260 --> 00:57:23,300
and usually that's about 6% of your gross revenue.

1199
00:57:23,300 --> 00:57:25,860
No problem, no fucking problem.

1200
00:57:25,860 --> 00:57:28,100
Cut me that deal.

1201
00:57:28,100 --> 00:57:29,060
Cut me the deal today.

1202
00:57:29,060 --> 00:57:30,820
I'll sign immediately.

1203
00:57:30,820 --> 00:57:32,740
I'd like it to be 4%, but it's okay.

1204
00:57:32,740 --> 00:57:34,180
We'll go for six if you want.

1205
00:57:34,940 --> 00:57:39,500
And 6% of zero is still zero at the moment.

1206
00:57:39,500 --> 00:57:40,860
But the minute I start making money,

1207
00:57:40,860 --> 00:57:44,260
as long as I can play unlimited ASCAP BMI licensed music,

1208
00:57:44,260 --> 00:57:45,300
you better believe it.

1209
00:57:45,300 --> 00:57:47,020
You better believe it all over that.

1210
00:57:47,020 --> 00:57:49,420
And it will make you more money

1211
